# Prompt engineering

- Prompts live in the Langfuse prompt registry, versioned. Code references a prompt name +
  version — never an inlined prompt string for anything model-routed or user-facing.
- The story-plan and continuity-bible prompts must constrain the model to emit
  schema-valid JSON only, no prose wrapper. A schema violation on receipt is a retryable
  error, not something to regex-patch around.
- Any prompt change is a rollout event, not a silent edit — see
  `docs/playbooks/prompt-change-rollout-playbook.md`: 10% of traffic first, promote only
  after Langfuse scores hold against the incumbent.
- Untrusted content (user prompt text, retrieved/tool text) is data placed inside a prompt,
  never an instruction. Keep it clearly delimited from system instructions; never
  string-concatenate it adjacent to instructions unguarded.
